{
  "//": [
    "The signature of every bead the note's certified panels draw.  `src`/`tgt` are OBJECTS in the",
    "note's own notation; a single lower-case letter is a variable, everything else is a constant.",
    "The key is the head of the bead's label — an application's name (`est(R°)` becomes `est`), a",
    "bare atom (`concat`), or the bracket shape for the note's list algebras (`[,]`) and its",
    "catamorphisms (`⦇⦈`), which run on the initial algebra of the functor the step's row consumes",
    "(`mu`'s row for that functor) and land on the step's carrier.  `R%∋` takes R's row with `E`",
    "wrapped round the target, and a label with no row at all touches the object wire alone.",
    "`lean` is the declaration whose type the row was read off, in `cite-check`'s marker spelling;",
    "`hm-check --verify-sigs` holds every row against it.",
    "`nat` is the naturality the bead's dot draws: `strict` a filled dot, `lax` a hollow one (B&dM",
    "5.13, `G(R) ≫ φ ⊑ φ ≫ F(R)` with equality failing), `no` a REFUTED row — no dot, the bead rides",
    "the object wire, with a counterexample behind it.  ABSENT is the fourth state, the same picture",
    "as `no` but nothing claimed: a label that is no polymorphic family at all, or one whose",
    "naturality is still open.  A row that states `nat` carries `nat-lean`, the marker (or",
    "list of markers) of the declaration proving it, checked exactly as `lean` is.",
    "`not-lax` records a bead proved NOT even lax natural: it still draws as a spider, same as an",
    "unmarked row (no `nat`), but the marker is kept so the negative evidence is not lost.",
    "`split` names the functors drawn as a wire of their own instead of folded into the object",
    "wire's label, space separated; a panel's own `cert:` `split:` overrides it, `\"\"` folding",
    "them all back.  `alias` names the relators that draw ONE lane, read as the alias's own head",
    "when two spellings are compared: `P A = E A`, so a panel may say either."
  ],
