  "spelling": {
    "//": "What each Lean head DENOTES, in the note's own object language: the key is the note object it stands for, with a variable for each of the head's object arguments, taken left to right. `list(x)` is a head the note draws as one `list` lane over its last argument; `list(list(x))` a Lean name that folds TWO of the note's lanes into one (`Sched` is a list of segments, which are lists); `x×y` a binary former; a key with no variable is a constant object. A head entry is the constant's FULL name, or `[name, i, …]` naming the argument positions the variables take when they are not the trailing ones (`RelProd.p 𝒜 a b self` carries its factors at 1 and 2). One head may appear under SEVERAL keys — `dTuple` is both the note's `L` and its `N`, two index functors at two lengths, and no Lean name tells them apart — and the match takes whichever the row asks for. `hm-check --verify-sigs` translates a cited declaration's type through this table and unifies it with the row; a head with no entry is a failure that names the head.",
